| `install sources` | `scripts/install_sources.py` prints the mirror config/project.json `install_sources` sets for one source alone on one line, and nothing for null, so `make fe-install`, `make fe-browsers` and each workflow's `pip install` or `npm ci` pass `--registry`, `PLAYWRIGHT_DOWNLOAD_HOST` or `--index-url` only when a mirror is set. | `make fe-install`; `make fe-browsers`; a workflow's install step | [`install_sources.python_index`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`install_sources.npm_registry`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`install_sources.browser_download_host`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`scripts/install_sources.py source`](settings.md#command-line-flags) | Refuses a URL that is not https or carries an `@`, `?`, `#`, backslash or invalid port with exit 14, never showing a value that holds an `@`, so a mirror's credential goes in the tool's own `pip.conf` or `.npmrc`. Not the scanner's mirror: `secrets.scanner.release_url`. Not a proxy: `HTTPS_PROXY` and `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS` pass through `child_env.names`. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md) | always |
